{"base_rate":0.583883751651255,"brier":0.15309801849405547,"bss":0.36987239531710125,"bss_hi":0.47362769619458744,"bss_lo":0.26391254635458655,"chart":{"base":[819.1,134.2],"fp":[314.9,271.3],"lead":"62,267.2 272,248.3 482,221.6 692,179.3","note":{"base":"skill 0.37 — higher than 65% of cities","fp":"low end +11pp, high end +14pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 79% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 10%; promised 97% → rained 83%"},"rel":"62.1,424.9 248.4,322 670.5,108.2"},"country":"NO","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11688243064729197,"ess":334.1878832243585,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Stavanger</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Stavanger rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>88%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>10%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nSTAVANGER - VALAND, 1.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.37, ranked 47 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(22&ndash;86) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>10%</b></td><td class='num'>147</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>10%</td><td class='num'><b>21%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>76</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>56%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>88%</b></td><td class='num'>383</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 5 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Stavanger</b> <span class=\"muted\">NO</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.37</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>22&ndash;86\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Stavanger &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Stavanger\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"58.07224489795918,382.0 93.754,322.85 235.326052631579,161.68421052631578 348.62901408450705,53.887323943661954 409.4397389033943,18.0 409.4397389033943,23.726109660574366 348.62901408450705,120.53521126760563 235.326052631579,238.31578947368422 93.754,368.35 58.07224489795918,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"169.4663143989432\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"169.4663143989432\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.07224489795918,347.3333333333333 93.754,304.65 235.326052631579,214.3684210526316 348.62901408450705,176.92957746478874 409.4397389033943,62.668407310704936\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 10% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 147 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.07224489795918\" cy=\"347.3333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 10%&amp;#10;It rained 21% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"93.754\" cy=\"304.65\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 76 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"235.326052631579\" cy=\"214.3684210526316\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 56% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"348.62901408450705\" cy=\"176.92957746478874\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 88% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 383 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.4397389033943\" cy=\"62.668407310704936\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(58%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Stavanger the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (0.45) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.13).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'>0.128</td><td class='num'>16.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>45%</td><td class='num'>0.386</td><td class='num'>10.7%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'>0.424</td><td class='num'>8.5%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'>0.450</td><td class='num'>5.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":58.97005,"lon":5.73332,"n":757,"n_cities":134,"name":"Stavanger","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0002040816326530612,"n":147,"obs":0.09523809523809523,"sig":true},{"hi":0.2480000000000004,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.10100000000000002,"n":80,"obs":0.2125,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6840000000000004,"lo":0.2480000000000004,"mean":0.500921052631579,"n":76,"obs":0.4605263157894737,"sig":false},{"hi":0.92,"lo":0.6840000000000004,"mean":0.8209859154929577,"n":71,"obs":0.5633802816901409,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.92,"mean":0.9927676240208878,"n":383,"obs":0.8772845953002611,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":1.5,"provisional":false,"rank":47,"rank_hi":86.02499999999998,"rank_lo":22.0,"reliability":0.016202956954742574,"resolution":0.10606403097041428,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"stavanger","station":"STAVANGER - VALAND","timezone":"Europe/Oslo"}